              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphisms"} cartesian morphisms
          %p
            Symbolically, preserving cartesian morphisms means that for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E:\mathcal{E}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:B \to p(E)
            morphism in the base, we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0(f)^*E \cong F_1(f^*E)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^*
            denotes reindexing.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0
              is the identity we recover the notion of morphism between fibrations over the same base (which are the 1-cells in
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fib}(\mathcal{B})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1
              induces a family of functors between fibers over the same object in the base.
          %h2#for_cloven_fibrations For cloven fibrations
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p'
            are assumed to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cloven+fibrations"} cloven fibrations
            %strong (cloven) fibred functor
            between them is assumed to preserve the cleavage, i.e. the choice of cartesian lifts.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The total category of a fibration supports a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} factorization system
            whose left class is comprised of vertical maps (those projecting to an isomorphism) and whose right class are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} cartesian maps
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
